      </span>
    </h3>
    <div data-pro-tab-id=3D"218887" class=3D"station-tabs-tabpanel" data-ty=
pe=3D"text">
      <div class=3D"station-tabs-tabcontent"><section id=3D"faq-template" s=
tyle=3D"max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; font-family: DM Sans, sans-serif;=
 line-height: 1.6;">
<details style=3D"border-top: 1px solid #e5e5e5; padding: 14px 0; transitio=
n: all .3s;">
<summary style=3D"cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; font-size: 18px; list-=
style: none; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;"><span style=3D=
"flex: 1;">What is a PEMF device and how does it work?</span> <span class=
=3D"arrow">=E2=96=BE</span></summary>
<div style=3D"margin-top: 10px; font-size: 15px;">A PEMF (Pulsed Electromag=
netic Field) device sends low-level electromagnetic pulses into the body to=
 stimulate cell activity and promote natural healing. These pulses can impr=
ove circulation, support tissue regeneration, reduce pain, and help the imm=
une response, using gentle frequencies similar to those found in nature.</d=
iv>
</details>
<details style=3D"border-top: 1px solid #e5e5e5; padding: 14px 0; transitio=
n: all .3s;">
<summary style=3D"cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; font-size: 18px; list-=
style: none; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;"><span style=3D=
"flex: 1;">What are the different types of PEMF devices?</span> <span class=
=3D"arrow">=E2=96=BE</span></summary>
<div style=3D"margin-top: 10px; font-size: 15px;">Common types include PEMF=
 mats for whole-body wellness, PEMF machines for targeted therapy (often in=
 clinics), PEMF coils for at-home full-body relaxation and pain relief, and=
 portable PEMF devices designed for daily use and sleep support.</div>
</details>
<details style=3D"border-top: 1px solid #e5e5e5; padding: 14px 0; transitio=
n: all .3s;">
<summary style=3D"cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; font-size: 18px; list-=
style: none; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;"><span style=3D=
"flex: 1;">What conditions can PEMF therapy help with?</span> <span class=
=3D"arrow">=E2=96=BE</span></summary>
<div style=3D"margin-top: 10px; font-size: 15px;">PEMF therapy may support =
soft-tissue and bone healing, improve sleep quality, boost circulation, red=
uce inflammation, relieve pain, and assist with low mood and immune functio=
n.</div>
</details>
<details style=3D"border-top: 1px solid #e5e5e5; padding: 14px 0; transitio=
n: all .3s;">
<summary style=3D"cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; font-size: 18px; list-=
style: none; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;"><span style=3D=
"flex: 1;">How do PEMF devices differ from each other?</span> <span class=
=3D"arrow">=E2=96=BE</span></summary>
<div style=3D"margin-top: 10px; font-size: 15px;">Devices vary by power (pu=
lse strength and depth), frequencies offered (to target different needs), w=
aveform (minimal impact on outcomes), and recommended treatment time based =
on intensity.</div>
</details>
<details style=3D"border-top: 1px solid #e5e5e5; padding: 14px 0; transitio=
n: all .3s;">
<summary style=3D"cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; font-size: 18px; list-=
style: none; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;"><span style=3D=
"flex: 1;">How do I choose the right PEMF device?</span> <span class=3D"arr=
ow">=E2=96=BE</span></summary>
<div style=3D"margin-top: 10px; font-size: 15px;">Match the device to your =
goal: condition to address, frequency range (generally higher for chronic i=
ssues, lower for acute), intensity needed for tissue depth, and preferred f=
ormat (mat, coil, machine, or portable unit).</div>
</details>
<details style=3D"border-top: 1px solid #e5e5e5; padding: 14px 0; transitio=
n: all .3s;">
<summary style=3D"cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; font-size: 18px; list-=
style: none; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;"><span style=3D=
"flex: 1;">Are PEMF devices safe to use?</span> <span class=3D"arrow">=E2=
=96=BE</span></summary>
<div style=3D"margin-top: 10px; font-size: 15px;">Yes, PEMF devices use low=
-level, non-invasive frequencies considered safe for most adults. They are =
not recommended for pregnant women or children, as effects for these groups=
 have not been established.</div>
</details>
<details style=3D"border-top: 1px solid #e5e5e5; border-bottom: 1px solid #=
e5e5e5; padding: 14px 0; transition: all .3s;">
<summary style=3D"cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; font-size: 18px; list-=
style: none; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;"><span style=3D=
"flex: 1;">How should I use a PEMF device as a beginner?</span> <span class=
=3D"arrow">=E2=96=BE</span></summary>
<div style=3D"margin-top: 10px; font-size: 15px;">Start with a short trial =
period to see how you respond. Use mats or low-intensity options for chroni=
c conditions or sleep support, and choose portable or targeted devices for =
localized, acute issues. Follow the manufacturer=E2=80=99s guidance for ses=
sion length and frequency.</div>
</details>
</section>
</div>
    </div>






















































































